1="556.3" y1="150.0" x2="578.3" y2="150.0" stroke="#A7AEC0" stroke-width="1.4"/><rect x="578.3" y="126.6" width="272" height="46.8" rx="23.4" fill="#1E2A5A"/><text x="714.3" y="157.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="22.1" font-weight="800" fill="#FFFFFF">Higher Rapport 3.0</text><text x="714.3" y="111.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="20.8" font-weight="800" fill="#5D4FC4">Mutual Growth</text><circle cx="556.3" cy="150.0" r="5.5" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#1E2A5A" stroke-width="3"/></svg></div><a class="fz-more" href="approach.html#higher-rapport">Learn more →</a></article><article class="sg-card sg-wide"><div class="txt"><span class="no">SOLUTION III</span><h3>3S Questioning Method</h3><p>A core approach in PLUSZONE Education that helps you see yourself objectively, clarify your direction, and take ownership of your life.</p><div class="acts"><a class="fz-more" href="approach.html#questioning">Learn more →</a></div></div><div class="fz-steps">
<div class="fz-step"><span class="n">S1</span><div><b>Self-Reflection</b><q>Why did I think and act that way?</q><small>Discovering the root causes of unconscious thoughts and emotions</small></div></div>
<div class="fz-step"><span class="n">S2</span><div><b>Setting Plus (+) Standards</b><q>Are my thoughts and actions Plus or Minus?</q><small>Reviewing my own standards and choosing the values to put into practice</small></div></div>
<div class="fz-step"><span class="n">S3</span><div><b>Standards into Action</b><q>So, what should I do now, and how?</q><small>Naturally putting the chosen standards into action</small></div></div>
</div></article></div></div></section><section class="fz-sec fz-prac-sec" id="practice"><div class="wrap"><div class="fz-prac has-pv rv"><div><span class="fz-tag"><b class="stp">STEP 2 · PRACTICE</b>FOR TEACHERS · FREE · NO SIGN-UP</span><h2>Rehearse Tomorrow’s Classroom Moments<br><em>with the 3S Method Today</em></h2><p>Not sure what to say when a student is late, upset, or in conflict with a friend? Practice the 3S (3-Step) Questioning Method with classroom situation cards and get instant AI feedback—or work through your own classroom concern right now. No sign-up required.</p><div class="fz-prac-acts"><a class="fz-btn" href="https://pluszone-edusolution.app/?lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start 3S Practice →</a><span class="fz-time"><svg class="clk" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg>One session takes about 3 minutes · 1 situation card · 3 questions</span><a class="fz-more" href="#videos">Next: see student stories ↓</a></div></div><div class="dm" role="group" aria-label="What would you say first?"><span class="dm-tag">1-minute try · Situation card</span><h3>What would you say first?</h3><p class="dm-sit">At break time, Minjun storms back into the classroom after arguing with a friend.</p><small class="dm-note">※ Student names are pseudonyms.</small><p class="dm-hint">Choose one</p><div class="dm-opts"><button type="button" class="dm-opt" aria-pressed="false" data-lbl="A fact-finding question first" data-fb="A natural reaction. But the moment we ask “who started it,” children tend to defend themselves. Hold the judgment for a moment and let the child look at their own feelings first." data-good="0">“Again? Who started it?”</button><button type="button" class="dm-opt" aria-pressed="false" data-lbl="The right answer, given first" data-fb="Not wrong at all. But when a lecture comes first, the child’s heart tends to close, and the standard stays “the teacher’s rule.” Try turning it into a question so the child sets the standard." data-good="0">“I told you not to fight with friends, didn’t I?”</button><button type="button" class="dm-opt" aria-pressed="false" data-lbl="The first 3S question: Self-Reflection" data-fb="A great start. You acknowledge the feeling and invite the child to look at their own thoughts and heart. Then continue like this:" data-good="1">“You look really upset. How did you feel at that moment?”</button></div><div class="dm-res" hidden aria-live="polite"><b class="lbl"></b><p></p><ol class="dm-seq" hidden><li><b>S1</b><span>“How did you feel at that moment?”</span></li><li><b>S2</b><span>“Were the words and actions that came from that feeling Plus or Minus?”</span></li><li><b>S3</b><span>“So, what could you do now for your friend?”</span></li></ol><div class="dm-acts"><button type="button" class="dm-again">Try another answer</button></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="fz-sec" id="videos"><div class="wrap">
<div class="fz-head c rv"><span class="fz-tag"><b class="stp">STEP 3 · SEE</b>STUDENT STORIES</span><h2>Student transformation<br><em>on video</em></h2><p>Short videos of real student guidance cases from the classroom.</p></div>
<div class="rv"><div class="vgrid">
