<!-- 영상 4: data-yt="" 안에 유튜브 주소(또는 영상 ID)를 넣으세요 -->
<article class="vcard" data-yt="FirNu_VuJw4"><button class="vplay" type="button" style="background-image:url(video4-poster.jpg)" aria-label="Play video: Case 4"><span class="vicon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="vsoon">Coming soon</span></button><div class="vtxt"><span class="vno">CASE 4</span><b>Learning to Lose Gracefully</b><p>Discovering that playing together matters more than winning, a student learned to manage the feeling of losing.</p></div></article></div></div>
<div class="fz-quotes rv">
<div class="fz-q"><b>“Youngchan, you’re doing so well lately!”</b><p>When a child who had lost friends through anger tried hard to be considerate, classmates were the first to pat him on the shoulder.</p><span>Understanding and forgiveness</span></div>
<div class="fz-q"><b>“I can’t control it on my own yet”</b><p>A child often late from gaming kept handing in the phone by choice, and by the second semester could manage alone.</p><span>The power to judge for oneself</span></div>
<div class="fz-q"><b>“Teacher, I held back my anger today!”</b><p>A child who came to the teacher alone every period grew into one who came with friends and a brighter face.</p><span>Friendships and emotions</span></div>
<div class="fz-q"><b>A child who brightened by helping others</b><p>A class president who only did his own work began helping classmates clean, and they chose him as their leader.</p><span>The value of love</span></div>
</div>
<p class="pseudo">※ All student names are pseudonyms.</p><div class="fz-center"><a class="fz-btn ghost" href="stories.html">More stories →</a></div>
</div></section><section class="fz-sec cs-sec" id="case"><div class="wrap"><div class="cs-top rv"><div class="fz-head"><span class="fz-tag">FROM REAL CLASSROOMS</span><h2>What it sounds like<br><em>in a real classroom</em></h2></div><a class="fz-more" href="stories.html#dialogues">All cases →</a></div><div class="cs-grid"><article class="cs-big rv"><span class="cs-who">Case 1 · Jinsu, 4th grade</span><h3>Honesty chosen with a red pencil</h3><p class="cs-sit">After the final exam, Jinsu claimed an answer had been marked wrong — but the answer, originally 1, had been changed to 4.</p><div class="cs-dlg"><p class="tc"><b>Teacher:</b> Jinsu, mark it yourself. A score you get by cheating isn’t your real ability. I hope you make the brave choice that lets you stand tall.</p><p class="act">(A moment later, Jinsu brings back the answer sheet with a cross on it.)</p><p class="tc"><b>Teacher:</b> Thank you for choosing honesty.</p></div><p class="cs-res"><b>What changed:</b> Jinsu left with a proud, bright face. It never happened again.</p></article><div class="cs-side"><a class="cs-s rv" href="stories.html#dialogues"><span class="cs-who">Case 2 · Cheolsu</span><b>A lie is a lie, even as a joke</b><p>“Why isn’t it right? Who would it hurt?” — questions instead of a lecture, and Cheolsu decided for himself.</p><span class="st-go">Read case →</span></a><a class="cs-s rv" href="stories.html#dialogues"><span class="cs-who">Case 3 · Beomsu, 6th grade</span><b>The real reason, heard by asking</b><p>Over a month of correction changed nothing. One genuinely curious question finally let him share what was inside.</p><span class="st-go">Read case →</span></a></div></div><p class="pseudo">* All student names are pseudonyms.</p></div></section><section class="fz-sec tv-sec" id="voices"><div class="wrap"><div class="cs-top rv"><div class="fz-head"><span class="fz-tag">TEACHER VOICES</span><h2>What teachers said<br><em>after our training</em></h2></div><a class="fz-more" href="stories.html#voices">More voices →</a></div><div class="tv-grid"><figure class="tv-q rv"><figcaption class="tv-t">The joy of the first child changed by questions</figcaption><blockquote>“Instead of teacher-centered discipline, I learned the questions students truly need to solve problems and grow in character, and came to know what real guidance is. I’ll never forget the joy of first changing a student with the 3S (3-Step) Questioning Method.”</blockquote><cite>— Kim ○○, elementary school teacher</cite></figure><figure class="tv-q rv"><figcaption class="tv-t">With a heart of helping and caring, not resentment</figcaption><blockquote>“I learned that guidance must go beyond simple discipline and address root causes based on value standards. Instead of my old habit of resenting students, I now understand their side first, with a heart of helping and caring.”</blockquote><cite>— Lee ○○, high school teacher</cite></figure></div></div></section><section class="fz-sec alt" id="people"><div class="wrap">
